  "public_instruction": "Clean all six designated dining and kitchen surfaces with the cleaning cloth without causing cross-contamination across surface stain tiers (rinsing the cloth in the kitchen sink resets its stain level), inspect and restock the closed dining room storage cabinet from the pantry supply shelf until it holds two bottles of apple juice, two bottles of tea, and two boxes of crackers (wiping the interior cabinet shelf clean before placing new items inside), close the cabinet doors, leave the wooden utility tray on a shelf, table, or counter, and finish empty-handed.",
  "public_context": [
    "Clean all six designated surfaces across the dining area and kitchen using the cleaning cloth: dining table and kitchen prep counter (Tier 1 light dust), kitchen island bar counter and interior shelf of the dining room storage cabinet (Tier 2 moderate dust), and cooking stove top and kitchen waste surround counter (Tier 3 heavy stains). Hygiene rule: wiping a surface sets the cloth stain level to at least that surface tier, and wiping a lower-tier surface while the cloth carries a higher-tier stain causes cross-contamination unless the cloth is rinsed (soaked) in the kitchen sink first to reset it to clean. At completion, leave the rinsed cleaning cloth resting on the kitchen prep counter.",
    "Open and inspect the closed storage cabinet in the dining room, and restock it using supplies from the pantry supply shelf in the living-room hallway until the cabinet holds two bottles of apple juice, two bottles of tea, and two boxes of crackers: the interior shelf of the cabinet must be wiped clean before any new supplies are placed inside, and both doors of the cabinet must be closed when finished.",
    "Leave the wooden utility tray resting on the pantry supply shelf, the dining table, or the kitchen bar counter, and finish the task with no object held in hand."
  ],
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "clean_dining_and_kitchen_surfaces",
      "text": "Clean all six designated surfaces across the dining area and kitchen using the cleaning cloth: dining table and kitchen prep counter (Tier 1 light dust), kitchen island bar counter and interior shelf of the dining room storage cabinet (Tier 2 moderate dust), and cooking stove top and kitchen waste surround counter (Tier 3 heavy stains). Hygiene rule: wiping a surface sets the cloth stain level to at least that surface tier, and wiping a lower-tier surface while the cloth carries a higher-tier stain causes cross-contamination unless the cloth is rinsed (soaked) in the kitchen sink first to reset it to clean. At completion, leave the rinsed cleaning cloth resting on the kitchen prep counter.",
      "terminal": [
        "surfaces_clean",
        "rag_returned"
      ],
      "constraints": [
        "no_cross_contamination"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restock_dining_cabinet",
      "text": "Open and inspect the closed storage cabinet in the dining room, and restock it using supplies from the pantry supply shelf in the living-room hallway until the cabinet holds two bottles of apple juice, two bottles of tea, and two boxes of crackers: the interior shelf of the cabinet must be wiped clean before any new supplies are placed inside, and both doors of the cabinet must be closed when finished.",
      "terminal": [
        "cabinet_stocked",
        "cabinet_closed"
      ],
      "constraints": [
        "cabinet_clean_before_stock_juice1",
        "cabinet_clean_before_stock_juice2",
        "cabinet_clean_before_stock_snack1",
        "cabinet_clean_before_stock_snack2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "carrier_parking_and_empty_hand",
      "text": "Leave the wooden utility tray resting on the pantry supply shelf, the dining table, or the kitchen bar counter, and finish the task with no object held in hand.",
      "terminal": [
        "tray_parked",
        "hand_empty"
      ]
    }
  ],
